From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: SC_MAXIMIZE leaves a hidden, already maximized window hidden and inactive

Microsoft Edge 154 for Windows crashed on every start once its window had
been maximized (David's Latitude 2026-10-06: "it does not start";
exception c0000005 at msedge.dll+0x2eeff68, a read at address 0xb0).
Chromium creates a browser window that last ran maximized with
WS_MAXIMIZE, hidden, and then sends it WM_SYSCOMMAND SC_MAXIMIZE
(views::Widget::Init's Maximize()) before its first tab exists; it shows
the window itself later with ShowWindow(SW_SHOWMAXIMIZED). Wine's
DefWindowProc turned that SC_MAXIMIZE into ShowWindow(SW_MAXIMIZE), which
showed and activated the empty window, and Edge's WM_ACTIVATE handler
(its "dual_engine.set_foreground_when_active" path) followed a pointer the
first tab sets. A hidden window that is maximized already has nothing to
change, so it now stays hidden and inactive until its program shows it;
visible windows maximize as before.

Test: test/hiddenmax-gate.sh with test/hiddenmax-probe.c (mutant
SG_MUTANT_HIDDEN_SC_MAXIMIZE).
---
--- a/dlls/win32u/defwnd.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/defwnd.c
@@ -1114,6 +1114,14 @@
         break;
 
     case SC_MAXIMIZE:
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_HIDDEN_SC_MAXIMIZE
+        /* A hidden window that is maximized already (created with
+         * WS_MAXIMIZE) has nothing to change: it stays hidden and inactive
+         * until its program shows it. Chromium's browser windows get
+         * SC_MAXIMIZE this way before their first tab exists, and Edge
+         * crashed in the WM_ACTIVATE that showing it here sent. */
+        if ((get_window_long( hwnd, GWL_STYLE ) & (WS_VISIBLE | WS_MAXIMIZE)) == WS_MAXIMIZE) break;
+#endif
         if (is_iconic(hwnd)) show_owned_popups( hwnd, TRUE );
         NtUserShowWindow( hwnd, SW_MAXIMIZE );
         break;
